# PSL release policy

Applies to work Luke requests. It does not authorize merging arbitrary,
unrequested PRs.

## Default finish

Unless Luke explicitly asks for review-only work, the finish is:
implemented → tested → merged into `main` → Production READY → verified.
Do not stop at "branch pushed" or ask for another routine merge approval.

This supersedes older task briefs or prompts that default to "push for
review only" or "no merge/deploy without approval". A current request that
explicitly says review-only, or withholds a specific authority, still wins.

## Before merging

- Use temporary branches and PRs internally when appropriate.
- Run the relevant tests, typecheck, lint on changed files, and build.
- Review the complete diff for unrelated changes. Never stage unrelated local
  files; preserve them and all secrets.
- Merge the requested work through its PR, pinned to the exact tested head
  SHA. If `main` or the branch moved, check the combined changes and rerun the
  affected checks before merging.
- Never force-push, bypass required checks, or weaken tests to release.

## After merging

- A Vercel build alone does not prove the application tests passed.
- Verify the resulting Production deployment: READY state, its commit SHA,
  and that the normal custom domain serves it. Only then report the work as
  live.
- Do not promote an old preview that omits newer `main` changes.

## Data, money, and permissions

- Database tests run only against the disposable test database, never
  Production.
- Production migrations need explicit authorization for the task, a review of
  the effective script, and a verified target. Stop if the migration would do
  more than what was reviewed.
- Code-release permission does not authorize new spending, destructive data
  operations, broader permissions, or public content.
- Do not turn off already-authorized, working automations just because
  another task originally shipped them disabled.

## Stopping and reporting

- Stop only for a real blocker, missing authority, or unresolved risk, and
  state exactly what blocked completion.
- Final report: live or not live, merge commit, tests, Production deployment,
  and any one-time activation still needed. Do not leave routine branch
  management to Luke.
